      "description": "Maintenance, Repair, and Sustainability Coordinator II - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Maintenance, Repair, and Sustainability Coordinator II Cookeville, TN, United States Job Description Description of Job Duty: Performs a variety of tasks in the installation, repair and maintenance of electrical systems and equipment.  Occasionally asked to assist in job functions outside of this purview. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Install and repair electrical wiring, fixtures, panels, circuit breakers, and other apparatus. Plan new or renovated existing installations to minimize waste of materials, provide access for future maintenance, and avoid unsightly, hazardous, and unreliable wiring. Install conduit, wire, and devices such as receptacles, switches, light fixtures, and other electrical apparatus. Test continuity of circuits to ensure electrical continuity and safety of components using test instruments. Work on electrical circuits carrying 600v or less. Inspect and test commercial machinery control equipment and systems; following blueprints and wiring schematics. Examine wiring for loose or faulty connections. Repairs electrical motors, controllers, and starters. Work with outside vendors to maintain elevators and perform periodic checks. Work with special events and athletic personnel to ensure uninterrupted electrical service. Operate equipment such as scissor lifts, articulating boom lifts, large trucks, trailer towing, scaffold construction and work, and any other equipment typical with electrical installation and maintenance. Must be comfortable working at heights up to 125ft and knowledgeable as to how to do so safely. Physical Demands: Work indoors and outdoors in all weather conditions. Must be able to lift heavy items up to 100 pounds and carry ladders. Must be able to walk often and at a considerable length. Must be able to climb stairs regularly. Work Hours: Typical hours are Monday through Friday, 7:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. Occasional overtime required. Adjusted work schedule may or may not be available upon request. Special Instructions: Other duties as assigned. Salary: Level S2, Grade 7. Benefits: The University offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the initial accumulation of one vacation day per month and one sick leave day per month, and thirteen University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent with two years of related professional experience. Must possess and maintain a valid driver's license. Ability to learn and willingness to be taught. Good attitude in a team environment. Preferred Qualifications: TN State e lectrical license. Completion of electrical apprenticeship program. Work experience in a variety of electrical and related fields. Reads and interprets blueprints, drawings and schematics. Experience in industrial/commercial electrical work. Basic knowledge of electrical diagnostic equipment. Familiarity with elevator and/or generator controls. Knowledge of work experience involving, or certification for low voltage/data installation and troubleshooting. Knowledge of work experience involving and/or certification for fire alarm installation and troubleshooting. Working knowledge of Telecommunication/IT installation and operation. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 26016 Posting Date 09/21/2026, 07:03 AM Grade 7 Screening Date: 10/21/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to 