      "description": "Administrative Services Coordinator II - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Administrative Services Coordinator II Cookeville, TN, United States Job Description Description of Job Duty: Serve as the departmental administrative assistant. Perform a wide variety of clerical duties which could be confidential in nature. Maintain departmental student files. Assist director, faculty, and advisors with a variety of student-related academic matters. Maintain departmental fiscal records and prepare various university forms associated with this responsibility. Function as the main point of contact between the School of Interdisciplinary Studies and other academic departments and off-campus programs. Maintain and update the SOIS website. Other duties as assigned. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Serve as the departmental receptionist/secretary. Support the director in daily administrative activities. Point of contact for on and off campus programs. Assist director, faculty, and advisors with a variety of student-related academic matters, issuing of enrollment permits, drop-add slips and course substitutions. Inputs classes into Coursedog and schedules classrooms. Maintain departmental fiscal records, process university requisitions for invoices and travel claims, prepare personnel and financial components and contracts, and reconcile monthly expenditures. Assist students with registration. Handle office correspondence and perform a wide variety of clerical duties which could be confidential in nature. Technology assistance with websites, social media, faculty assistance. Maintain departmental student files, faculty academic and employment files. Supervise student workers in the accomplishment of the above tasks and office-related assignments. Serve as the central point of contact with off-campus sites and related off-campus staff. Physical Demands: Those typical to an office environment. Work Hours: Typical hours are 8:00 am - 4:30 pm. Special Instructions: Applicants are required to electronically upload a resume and complete contact information for three professional references at time of application. References will be contacted at a later date. Submission of materials is the applicant's responsibility. Applications without all required materials are incomplete and will not be considered. Salary: Level S2, Grade 6. Benefits: Tennessee Tech offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the initial accumulation of one vacation day per month, one sick leave day per month, and thirteen (13) University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent. Two years of general office experience. Working proficiency with software such as Microsoft Outlook, Word and Excel. Ability to work with minimum supervision. Ability to work in a fast-paced and flexible environment. Ability to effectively supervise student workers. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Prior experience in an academic environment with basic accounting skills. Experience with Talon (Oracle) and Coursedog. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 26030 Posting Date 09/21/2026, 08:38 AM Grade 6 Screening Date: 10/01/2026 Similar Jobs Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Re