    "https://fa-eygi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/26039": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Assistant Professor Cookeville, TN, United States Job Description Description of Job Duty: The Department of Decision Sciences and Management at Tennessee Tech University invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning August 1, 2027. Teaching responsibilities will focus primarily on Human Resource Management. Preference will be given to candidates who can also contribute to the department’s teaching needs in Strategic Management, International Management, or related areas. Minimum qualifications include 1) a doctoral degree in Business Administration, Human Resources, Strategic Management, or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited institution (ABDs nearing completion may be considered if the degree will be granted by July 31, 2027), 2) excellent teaching and communication skills, 3) an ability to publish research in peer-reviewed journals. Preferred qualifications include 1) experience teaching in-person, online, and/or hybrid courses, 2) experience engaging students in meaningful experiential activities, 3) ability to contribute to strategic college, university, and societal initiatives, and 4) related professional work experience and/or related professional certifications. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Responsibilities for the position may include teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels and teaching in face-to-face and online environments. All tenure-track faculty in the College of Business are expected to maintain a level of scholarly activity to qualify as Scholarly Academics in AACSB reporting. The College of Business values engagement with the local and regional business communities, as well as service to the department, university, and profession. Our department is home to approximately 500 students, and we offer majors in Business Management, Business & Information Technology, and Business AI & Analytics. Within Business Management, we offer concentrations in General Management, Human Resource Management, and Operations & Supply Chain Management. We also provide graduate courses to support the College's MBA Program and graduate-level certificates. Tennessee Tech provides impact through its engaged students, dedicated faculty, and career-ready graduates known for their creativity, tenacity, and analytical approach to problem solving. As a STEM-infused, comprehensive institution, Tennessee Tech delivers enduring education, impactful research, and collaborative service that creates, advances, and applies knowledge to expand opportunity and economic competitiveness. Physical Demands: Those typical of an office and classroom environment. Special Instructions: Applicants will be required to apply online at jobs.tntech.edu and electronically upload a letter of application, curriculum vitae, copies of transcripts (official transcripts for all degrees conferred required upon hire), teaching philosophy, and contact information for three professional references at time of application. References will be contacted via email to provide a reference letter if selected for interview. Submission of materials is the applicant's responsibility. Applications without all required materials are incomplete and will not be considered. Initial screening will begin November 24, 2026; open until filled. Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Benefits Info: Benefits include the accumulation of one (1) sick leave day per month and thirteen (13) University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Deferred income and benefits over 12 months. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Minimum qualifications include 1) a doctoral degree in Business Administration, Human Resources, Strategic Management, or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited institution (ABDs nearing completion may be considered if the degree will be granted by July 31, 2027), 2) excellent teaching and communication skills, 3) an ability to publish research in peer-reviewed journals. Preferred Qualifications: Preferred qualifications include 1) experience teaching in-person, online, and/or hybrid courses, 2) experience engaging students in meaningful experiential activities, 3) ability to contribute to strategic college, university, and societal initiatives, and 4) related professional work experience and/or related professional certifications. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 26039 Posting Date 09/21/2026, 08:53 AM Grade 0 Screening Date: 11/24/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 242 E. 10th Street, Cookeville, TN, 38505, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Assistant Professor Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 08/12/2026 Trending Full-time, tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor rank starting in August 2027. Assistant Professor Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/15/2026 Be the First to Apply Assistant Professor of Violin/Viola\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Assistant Professor Cookeville, TN, United States and 1 more Posted on 09/11/2026 Be the First to Apply Teach courses, perform research, and fulfill service mission for the Department of Counseling and Psychology.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Assistant Professor of Clarinet Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/21/2026 Be the First to Apply The School of Music at Tennessee Tech University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Clarinet, beginning August 1, 2027.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. See More Jobs Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Assistant Professor - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers loaded"
