    "https://fa-eygi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/26028": {
      "title": "Temporary Help Non-Exempt",
      "description": "Temporary Help Non-Exempt - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Temporary Help Non-Exempt Cookeville, TN, United States Job Description Description of Job Duty: We are looking for a dedicated and organized individual to join our student success center as a temporary part-time administrative associate. You will play a vital role in supporting students, answering their queries, and ensuring a smooth experience. This role involves a range of administrative tasks and the chance to contribute to our social media presence and recruitment efforts. Tennessee Technological University is an equal opportunity affirmative action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Answering incoming phone calls and providing excellent customer service to students and visitors. Generating and analyzing reports to support student success initiatives. Assisting students with their inquiries and providing accurate information. Scheduling appointments for students and ensuring efficient time management. Updating and maintaining recruitment materials and resources. Assisting with social media content creation and engagement strategies. Collaborating with the team to ensure a positive and inclusive student experience. Performing data entry and record-keeping tasks as required. Assisting with event coordination and setup when needed. Other administrative duties as assigned by the supervisor. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent; some college education preferred. Minimum 1 year of experience in an administrative role, preferably in an educational setting. Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and basic computer skills. Ability to work independently and manage multiple tasks simultaneously. Customer service orientation with a friendly and helpful attitude. Basic knowledge of social media platforms and content creation. Willingness to learn and adapt to new technologies and systems. Ability to maintain confidentiality and adhere to university policies. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 26028 Posting Date 09/18/2026, 09:03 AM Grade 0 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 200 W. 10th Street, Cookeville, TN, 38505, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Temporary Help Exempt Cookeville, TN, United States and 1 more Posted on 09/22/2026 Be the First to Apply The Crossville Research Center (CRC) Administrative Services Specialist II (Temporary) serves as the primary point of contact for Center partners who contact or visit the office, providing guidance on CRC policies, processes and service requests while directing clients to appropriate staff. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Temporary Help Non-Exempt - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers loaded"
