    "https://fa-eygi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/26036": {
      "title": "Administrative Services Coordinator III",
      "description": "Administrative Services Coordinator III - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Administrative Services Coordinator III Cookeville, TN, United States Job Description Description of Job Duty: Provide administrative support to the Director, Accountant, Design Manager(2), CAD Operator, and Project Managers (5). Coordinate/manage bids, contracts, insurance reporting, Physical Facility Inventory and Survey, F&A Capital Budget submittals, State Architect and State Building Commission submittals. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Performs general bookkeeping functions including preparation of departmental requisitions for payment and budget revisions. Maintain records of expenditures, account balance, billing and payable files, and records. Responsible for coordinating lease and land transaction requests, submittals and reports. Annually audits insurance reports, revises, as needed, and submits to TN Risk Management. Compiles capital budget data and prepares for submission to THEC and F&A. Compiles data and completes reports and submits to THEC, F&A and other federal, state, and local government regulatory agencies. Provides administrative support for the Director, Design Manager, and CAD Operator. Composes routine correspondence, proofs, edits and revises materials for general distribution. Types various reports, memos, letters, etc. Routinely handles confidential information. Coordinates the RFP process. Provides clerical support for the RFP process. Prepares RFP’s for design, construction and leases. Posts RFP’s on website, receives RFP’s, reviews for compliance and distributes to evaluation team. Responsible for coordinating bid openings. Receives bid documents, reviews bids for standard compliance, assigns bid dates, and enters information into the Project Information Tracking System (PITS). Verifies bidder’s contractor license for award. Provides support for contract submittals to OSA for approval. Enters award, approval dates and other project information into PITS. Send notices of pre-construction conferences. Receives Insurance Certificates from contractors, verifies insurance coverage amounts and enters into PITS. Maintains department website in compliance with SBC, OSA, and THEC requirements. Assists with updating processes, procedures, designer’s manual and work process flow charts for the department. Supervises student worker, reviews time sheets and prepares student payroll. Assists faculty, staff, students and general public with program and services offered through the department. Explains policies and procedures. Physical Demands: Those typical of an office environment. Work Hours: Typical hours are Monday-Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Special Instructions: Applicants are required to electronically upload a resume and complete contact information for three professional references at time of application.  References will be contacted at a later date. Submission of materials is the applicant's responsibility. Applications without all required materials are incomplete and will not be considered. Salary: Level S3, Grade 8. Benefits: Tennessee Tech offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the initial accumulation of one vacation day per month, one sick leave day per month, and thirteen (13) University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: High School diploma or equivalent. Four years of related professional experience or an associate's degree (60 credit hours) with two years of related experience. Experience with purchasing, bid logistics management and experience compiling RFP’s. Computer literacy in software such as Microsoft Office Suite; database and spreadsheet applications. Ability to communicate effectively. Ability to maintain professional working relationships with administration, faculty, students, designers and contractors. Preferred Qualifications: Three to five years of relevant office experience. Experience with software such as Oracle or other higher education enterprise system. Experience in a higher education setting. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 26036 Posting Date 09/18/2026, 02:18 PM Grade 8 Screening Date: 10/05/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 220 W. 10th Street, Cookeville, TN, 38505, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Administrative Services Coordinator II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/21/2026 Responsible for all support functions related to the students, faculty, staff of the School of Interdisciplinary Studies.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Administrative Services Coordinator I Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/11/2026 Manage and support the main office area of University Housing and Residential Life.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Administrative Services Coordinator III - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers loaded"
