    "https://fa-eygi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/26029": {
      "title": "Director/Professor of Human Ecology",
      "description": "Director/Professor of Human Ecology - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Director/Professor of Human Ecology Cookeville, TN, United States Job Description Description of Job Duty: Tennessee Tech University invites applications for the position of Director in the School of Human Ecology at the rank of Associate Professor or Full Professor. This is a full-time, twelve-month, tenured position. The Director serves as the chief academic and administrative officer of the School, providing visionary, strategic, and entrepreneurial leadership to advance its mission in alignment with the University’s commitment to student success, academic excellence, innovation, and community engagement. This is an opportunity to lead a multidisciplinary School at a pivotal moment of growth and to elevate its impact across the state, region, and nation. The School of Human Ecology offers two undergraduate majors and four programs of study, including Human Ecology (Human Development and Family Science; Nutrition and Dietetics), Design Studies (Architecture and Interior Design; Fashion Merchandising and Design), and graduate programs in Child Life and Community Health and Nutrition. These programs are uniquely positioned to address critical societal challenges related to health, well-being, families, and the built environment. The successful candidate will articulate and implement a bold strategic vision that enhances program quality, expands enrollment, strengthens external partnerships, and elevates the School’s visibility and reputation. The Director will work collaboratively with university leadership, faculty, and external stakeholders to position the School as a regional and national leader in human ecology education and applied scholarship. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: This is a twelve-month, full-time position. The Director will provide transformational leadership for the School of Human Ecology, including long-range strategic planning, program growth, and alignment with university priorities focused on student success, innovation, and workforce readiness. The Director will lead the school in establishing and achieving measurable goals that advance excellence in teaching, scholarly activity, community engagement, and student outcomes, while directing all academic and administrative operations, including preparation and defense of the annual budget, development of fee structures, and advancement of new academic programs and strategic initiatives that respond to emerging societal and workforce needs. The Director will serve as a leader in academic innovation, working collaboratively with faculty to ensure curricula remain current and aligned with accreditation standards and industry expectations, including those associated with the American Association of Family and Consumer Sciences, and will oversee accreditation, assessment, and continuous improvement processes. The role includes recruiting, supporting, and retaining a diverse and high-performing faculty and staff while fostering a culture of excellence, collaboration, accountability, and professional growth. The Director will advance student success and engagement through experiential learning, internships, community-based learning, and career readiness initiatives aligned with Tennessee Tech’s strategic priorities. The position also requires expanding the School’s reach and impact through strategic partnerships with local, state, and national agencies, clinical organizations, industry partners, and professional associations, including facilitating contractual agreements that enhance student opportunities and program relevance. The Director will lead efforts to secure external funding, philanthropic support, and resource development, including grants and partnerships that strengthen academic programs and infrastructure, and will advocate effectively for the School’s priorities within the University and to external audiences. Additionally, the Director will promote interdisciplinary collaboration across colleges and units, support the development and expansion of innovative instructional modalities such as online and hybrid graduate programs, and contribute to teaching within undergraduate and graduate programs, as well as advising student organizations as appropriate. The Director will represent the school in university governance, professional organizations, and community engagement activities to enhance its visibility and reputation and will perform other duties as assigned. Physical Demands: Those typical of any classroom-type environment or office environment. Special Instructions: All applicants will be required to electronically upload a (1) cover letter, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) administrative philosophy and vision for the School of Human Ecology, (4) teaching philosophy, (5) copies of transcripts (official transcripts for all degrees conferred required upon hire), and (6) email contact information for three professional references who will be contacted to provide a reference letter if the candidate is selected for interview. Initial review of applications will begin November 16, 2026; position open until filled. Submission of materials is the applicant’s responsibility. Applications without all required materials will be deemed incomplete and will not be considered. Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Benefits Information: Tennessee Tech offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the accumulation of one (1) sick leave day per month and thirteen (13) University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Qualifications Required Qualifications: An earned doctoral degree from an accredited institution in family and consumer sciences, human ecology, nutrition and dietetics, human development and family science, or a closely related field is required, with at least one degree in family and consumer sciences or human ecology. The successful candidate must meet the requirements for tenure and appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or higher in the School of Human Ecology. A minimum of six years of full-time teaching experience in an accredited program in human ecology or family and consumer sciences is required, along with demonstrated experience in student success, curriculum development, academic program administration, accreditation processes, and program assessment. The candidate must also have a strong record of effective teaching, scholarship, and service, with evidence of excellent interpersonal and communication skills, professional integrity, and the ability to lead and collaborate effectively within an academic environment. Prior administrative leadership experience is required, including demonstrated success in strategic planning, budgeting, faculty and staff evaluation, and program development. Preferred Qualifications: The candidate should have a record of effectively building external partnerships, securing funding, and advancing academic initiatives at scale. Evidence of leadership within professional organizations and the ability to enhance the visibility, reputation, and impact of an academic unit are highly desirable. In addition, experience with innovative and technology-enhanced instruction, including the development and delivery of online and hybrid academic programs, is preferred. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 26029 Posting Date 09/17/2026, 11:06 AM Grade 0 Screening Date: 11/16/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 715 Quadrangle, Cookeville, TN, 38505, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Director/Professor of Human Ecology - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers loaded"
