    "https://fa-eygi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/26015": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Horticultural Science",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Horticultural Science - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Assistant Professor of Horticultural Science Cookeville, TN, United States Job Description Description of Job Duty: The School of Agriculture in the College of Agriculture and Human Ecology at Tennessee Tech University invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Horticultural Science. This is a full-time, 9-month tenure-track position with responsibilities in teaching (50%), research (45%), and service (5%). Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: The successful candidate will develop a nationally recognized teaching and research program in horticultural science using a multidisciplinary approach. The responsibilities of the position include: Teach both undergraduate and graduate level courses in horticulture including nursery production and management, landscaping, floriculture, plant propagation, greenhouse management, and controlled environment horticulture. Advise students and collaborate with organizations, agencies, and schools for placement of students in internships and projects to develop critical skill sets. Conduct innovative basic and/or applied horticultural science research under field, controlled environment and laboratory conditions through independent and collaborative efforts with other faculty within the college, university, and other institutions. Write grant proposals and obtain external funding to support his or her research program. Publish in peer-reviewed journals in his or her discipline. Contribute to the school/college/university through service activities. Physical Demands: Those typical of an office/classroom environment. Special Instructions: All applicants will be required to electronically upload: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Copy of Transcripts (official transcripts will be required upon hire) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Plan Email contact information for three references who will be contacted at the time of interview selection to provide a reference letter. Questions should be directed to: Dr. Michael Nattrass, Interim Director and Associate Professor, School of Agriculture, P.O. Box 5034, Tennessee Tech University, Cookeville, TN 38505, E-mail: mnattrass@tntech.edu. Phone: 931-372-3012. Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Benefits: Tennessee Tech offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the accumulation of one (1) sick leave day per month and thirteen (13) University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: An earned Ph.D. degree, or ABD, from an accredited institution in in horticulture with an emphasis on nursery production and management, plant science, or dendrology. Candidates from other closely related fields must demonstrate substantial, documented nursery production experience to be considered. Substantial, hands-on experience in nursery crop production, propagation, and/or nursery/landscape management systems, gained through research, industry, or extension work. Demonstrated ability and research experiences to conduct horticultural science research in relevant areas using both traditional and modern technologies. Record of publication in peer-reviewed academic journals. Evidence of ability to pursue and obtain extramural funding through grant proposals. A strong background and experience in experimental design of field/laboratory and greenhouse trials, data management, and statistical analysis. Excellent written and oral communication skills in English. Strong interests in undergraduate and graduate teaching and advising. Preferred Qualifications: Documented evidence of individual and/or collaborative research and teaching in horticultural science and nursery & landscape management that have resulted in peer-reviewed publications. Post-doctoral experience in horticulture or nursery & landscape management. Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching, including online/hybrid modalities. Demonstrated ability to communicate and work collaboratively and effectively with faculty, staff, students, other academic programs, stakeholders, and agencies. Demonstrated ability to conduct program planning, implementation, and evaluation. Demonstrated ability or potential to provide effective academic and career advising to students. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 26015 Posting Date 09/11/2026, 06:59 AM Grade 0 Screening Date: 11/09/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 715 Quadrangle, Cookeville, TN, 38505, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Assistant Professor - Computer Science Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 12/10/2025 Trending The Department of Computer Science is seeking applicants to fill one tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning August 1, 2026.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Assistant Professor Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/21/2026 The Department of Decision Sciences and Management at Tennessee Tech University invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning August 1, 2027. \n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Assistant Professor Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 08/12/2026 Trending Full-time, tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor rank starting in August 2027. Assistant Professor Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/15/