    "https://fa-eygi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/26017": {
      "title": "Budget Planning and Management Coordinator II",
      "description": "Budget Planning and Management Coordinator II - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Budget Planning and Management Coordinator II Cookeville, TN, United States Job Description Description of Job Duty: Obtains, pays, and receives invoices, monthly account and procard/travel reconciliation, control of expenditures from accounts, budget revision creation, and similar tasks. Maintains and reconciles various departmental and college indexes. Log transactions and reconcile numerous college and departmental accounts. Submits travel estimates on behalf of travelers through internal college forms to supervisor for college review. Initiates hiring paperwork for faculty, graduate students, adjuncts, temporary employees, etc. Receive, log, and deliver deposits. Assist in drafting contracts to be used in conjunction with external partners. Independently manages special projects assigned by the supervisor. Other duties as assigned. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Obtains, pays, and receives invoices, monthly account and procard/travel reconciliation, control of expenditures from accounts, budget revision creation, and similar tasks. Maintains and reconciles various departmental and college indexes. Log transactions and reconcile numerous college and departmental accounts. Submits travel estimates on behalf of travelers through internal college forms to supervisor for college review. Initiates hiring paperwork for faculty, graduate students, adjuncts, temporary employees, etc. Receive, log, and deliver deposits. Assist in drafting contracts to be used in conjunction with external partners. Independently manages special projects assigned by the supervisor. Other duties as assigned. Physical Demands: The position requires sedentary to light physical work which may include but not be limited to: sitting at a desk for extended periods of time in a climate controlled environment, use of typical office equipment (telephone, computer, copier, scanner, fax), close visual work, sufficient hearing and speech to communication via in person, telephone and virtually, as well as light lifting, outdoor exposure during college events, and mobility across campus. Work Hours: Typical hours are Monday-Friday, 8:00 am - 4:30 pm. Special Instructions: Applicants are required to electronically upload a cover letter, resume and complete contact information for three professional references at time of application. References will be contacted at a later date. Submission of materials is the applicant's responsibility. Applications without all required materials are incomplete and will not be considered. Salary: Level S2, Grade 6. Salary commensurate with experience. Benefits: Tennessee Tech offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the initial accumulation of one vacation day per month, one sick leave day per month, and thirteen (13) University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and a minimum of two years clerical or related experience. Ability to interpret and follow office policies and procedures. Ability to establish and maintain positive working relationships with students, faculty and other personnel. Evidence of typing ability, computer skills and ability to use word processing and other software. Preferred Qualifications: A bachelors degree or financial experience especially in a university setting are preferred. Experience using Talon and/or Adobe Acrobat is also preferred. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 26017 Posting Date 09/11/2026, 06:53 AM Grade 6 Screening Date: 09/25/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors