      "title": "Academic Program Management Specialist II",
      "description": "Academic Program Management Specialist II - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Academic Program Management Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Job Description Description of Job Duty: Provide support for the mechanical and nuclear engineering programs' improvement and accreditation (ABET, SACS, MS and PhD program reviews). Increase the visibility of the MNE Department and its positive image among prospective and current students, employers, alumni, campus community, and the general public. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Meets with prospective students and their families during VIP campus visits, providing information about the department and its programs. Also helps coordinate major recruitment events such as the Fall Preview and Spring Showcase, ensuring that visitors have a welcoming and informative experience while learning about the opportunities available in the department. Leads communications, outreach, and public relations efforts to enhance the visibility of the Mechanical and Nuclear Engineering programs. This includes preparing departmental newsletters, magazines and using social media to highlight student achievements, faculty accomplishments, departmental events, and program strengths. Assists with planning and coordinating External Advisory Board meetings, departmental meetings, and alumni engagement activities. Helps with meeting logistics, communications, and follow-up, and records and maintains meeting minutes to ensure accurate documentation and continuity of departmental initiatives. Provides support for continuous program improvement and accreditation efforts within the Mechanical and Nuclear Engineering program. Assists with collecting and organizing data for ABET accreditation, MS and PhD program reviews. Plans and organizes departmental social and cultural events in coordination with the Chair. Also advises and supports ME student organizations by assisting with event planning, activities, and initiatives that enhance student engagement and strengthen the sense of community within the department. Manages the department’s display cases and hallway bulletin boards, website and helping highlight student achievements, departmental news, and important announcements. Physical Demands: Those typical of an office environment. Work Hours: Typical hours are Monday-Friday, 8:00 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. Additional hours if/when needed. Occasional travel to Outreach Events required. Special Instructions: Applicants are required to electronically upload a cover letter, resume, copy of transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire), and complete contact information for three references. References will be contacted at a later date. Submission of materials is the applicant’s responsibility. Applications without all required materials are incomplete and will not be considered. Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Level P2, Grade 10. Benefits Information: The University offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the accumulation of two vacation days per month, one sick leave day per month, and thirteen University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited institution in Business, Communications, or related field and three years of related experience. In-depth knowledge of computers and software. Experience in maintaining and updating websites and social media sites. Ability to analyze and report data in readable form with graphs and graphics. Evidence of excellent oral and written communication skills and presentation skills. Preferred Qualifications: Three years of software related experience (Banner, Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Access, ARGOS). Two years of experience in communications and/or public outreach. Two years of general business experience or MBA degree. Ability to plan and organize outreach and educational campaigns. Ability to work effectively with students, faculty and alumni from a diverse background. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 26004 Posting Date 09/01/2026, 07:10 AM Grade 10 Screening Date: 09/21/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 115 W. 10th Street, Cookeville, TN, 38505, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Academic Advising Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 05/21/2026 Academic advisor for undergraduate students.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Budget Planning and Management Coordinator II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/11/2026 The Budget Planning and Management Coordinator II (Financial Associate II) provides financial and administrative support within the Dean's office in the College of Emerging & Integrative Studies. Responsibilities include processing financial transactions, monitoring budgets and expenditures, reconciling accounts, preparing financial reports, assisting with purchasing and travel activities, and ensuring compliance with university policies and procedures. The position works closely with their supervisor, faculty, staff, and university departments to provide accurate, timely, and effective financial support.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Academic and Client Technologies Specialist III Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 07/06/2026 The goal of this position is to partner with academic and administrative units of the assigned area of campus to proactively assess and address needs, ensuring alignment with ACT and ITS policies.  Act as a trusted advisor within the university community, guiding departments through technology adoption, lifecycle management, and continuous improvement initiatives. Budget Planning and Management Specialist III Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 08/26/2026 The overall purpose of this position is to assist the University’s Budget Office with all budgetary matters and specifically with the position budgeting and control functions of more than 2,800 employees.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. See More Jobs Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Academic Program Management Specialist II - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers loaded"
