    "https://fa-eygi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/25991": {
      "title": "Budget Planning and Management Specialist III",
      "description": "Budget Planning and Management Specialist III - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Budget Planning and Management Specialist III Cookeville, TN, United States Job Description Description of Job Duty: Assisting in the preparation and submission of all the university $500M budgets to the TTU Board of Trustees, the Tennessee Board of Regents (TBR), and the Tennessee Higher Education Commission (THEC) and following TBR guidelines for the October Revised and Proposed Budget cycles and adhere to funding requirements for all position controls., Providing support and appropriate solutions to all levels of university faculty and staff relative to budget issues and working closely with Human Resources and departments regarding position funding. Provide monthly reports to President's Office, Grant Accounting and Human Resources., Responsible for setup up and maintaining the budget/position control segment of Banner HR for more than 2,800 employees., Assisting in providing budget analyses and projections to be used by the University's administration for critical resource allocation planning, this includes implementation of the University Wide Strategic Lapse Salary process multiple times throughout the year that provides funding for important initiatives., Processing paperwork necessary to appoint benefit eligible employees, adjuncts, and graduate assistants including setting up the budget for permanent positions and new position requests in compliance with polices and state guidelines., Work with Cash Management as back up for Bank Reconciliation to provide assurance of cross training and compliance with state audit. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Responsible to the Director for Budgeting, Planning, Reporting and Analysis for 1) Assisting in the preparation and submission of all the university $500M budget for Proposed, Revised and Current Estimate budget cycles to the TTU Board of Trustees, the Tennessee Board of Regents (TBR), and the Tennessee Higher Education Commission (THEC); 2) Providing support and appropriate solutions to all levels of university faculty and staff relative to budget issues and working closely with Human Resources and departments regarding position funding. Provide monthly reports to President's Office, Grant Accounting and Human Resources. ; 3) responsible for setup up and maintaining the budget/position control segment of Banner HR for more than 2,800 employees; 4) Assisting in providing budget analyses and projections to be used by the University's administration for critical resource allocation planning, this includes implementation of the University Wide Strategic Lapse Salary process multiple times throughout the year that provides funding for important initiatives; 5) following TBR guidelines for the October Revised and Proposed Budget cycles and adhere to funding requirements; 6) Assisting to create and reconcile monthly budget revisions; 7) Processing paperwork necessary to appoint benefit eligible employees, adjuncts, and graduate assistants including setting up the budget for permanent positions and new position requests in compliance with polices and state guidelines; 8) serve as the Business Office back-up for the monthly Cash management Bank Reconciliation function to provide assurance of cross training and compliance with state audit 9) performing all other duties as assigned. Physical Demands: Those typical of an office environment. Work Hours: Typical hours are Monday-Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Additional hours if/when needed. Special Instructions: Applicants are required to electronically upload a cover letter, resume, copy of transcripts (official transcripts may be required upon hire), and complete contact information for three references. References will be contacted at a later date, and letters of recommendation may be requested at a later date. Submission of materials is the applicant's responsibility. Applications without all required materials are incomplete and will not be considered. Salary: Level P3, Grade 13. Benefits: The University offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the accumulation of two vacation days per month and one sick leave day per month, and thirteen University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in Business Administration, Accounting, Finance, or similar type program(s) related to budgeting, planning, reporting and analysis. Four years of related professional experience. Demonstrated expert level utilizing software such as Microsoft Office Suite, especially Excel. Excellent communication and customer service skills. Strong computing, organizational, analytical, and critical thinking skills. Demonstrated ability to work as a team member. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in Business Administration, Accounting, Finance, or similar type program(s) related to budgeting, planning, reporting and analysis. Higher Education experience. Banner or similar higher-education ERP experience. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 25991 Posting Date 08/26/2026, 08:25 AM Grade 13 Screening Date: 09/18/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 1 Williams L Jones Dr, Cookeville, TN, 38505, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Budget Planning and Management Coordinator II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/11/2026 The Budget Planning and Management Coordinator II (Financial Associate II) provides financial and administrative support within the Dean's office in the College of Emerging & Integrative Studies. Responsibilities include processing financial transactions, monitoring budgets and expenditures, reconciling accounts, preparing financial reports, assisting with purchasing and travel activities, and ensuring compliance with university policies and procedures. The position works closely with their supervisor, faculty, staff, and university departments to provide accurate, timely, and effective financial support.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Capital Projects Specialist III Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 03/12/2026 Serve as a University liaison and Owner's Representative between the Board of Trustees, General Contractors, campus personnel and design professionals for capital maintenance and construction projects. Financial Aid Specialist III Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/24/2026 Be the First to Apply The overall purpose of this job is to ensure compliance with federal regulations is being practiced and in conjunction with Tennessee Tech’s institutional policies and procedures. \n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Academic Program Management Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/01/2026 Provide support for the mechanical engineering program development and accreditation (ABET, SACS, MS and PhD program reviews). Increase the visibility of the M.E. Department and its positive image among prospective and current students, employers, alumni, campus community, and the general public.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. See More Jobs Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end 