      "title": "Public Relations Specialist II",
      "description": "Public Relations Specialist II - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Public Relations Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Job Description Description of Job Duty: Lead the development and execution of strategic communications, engagement, and stewardship initiatives that strengthen relationships with alumni, donors, and other key constituents. This position oversees Advancement communications across print, digital, email, web, and social media platforms; manages donor stewardship communications; and supports the University's fundraising and engagement goals through effective messaging, content development, and leadership within Crawford Alumni Center. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Under the direction of the Executive Director for the Crawford Alumni Center (CAC), this position will oversee all print and electronic communication related to engagement and stewardship, including print, digital, email, web, and social media platforms. Develop an Advancement communications calendar. Create all original copy for University Advancement communications including but not limited to: engagement pieces; solicitations for direct mail, email, and social media; speechwriting for events, stewardship pieces such as Gratitude, Impact, and Alumnus newsletter, etc.; other stewardship pieces as assigned; establish and manage stewardship-related initiatives including acknowledgements, recognition, and ongoing communications with past and current donors to enhance their relationship with the University and Foundation in an effort to increase the likelihood of continued contributions. Manage CAC social media, including creating content, scheduling, and posting. Manage Advancement email platform by drafting and sending all alumni and donor related emails, as requested from university departments. Provide support to Advancement events by attending and participating as needed. Physical Demands: Those typical of an office environment. Work Hours: Typical hours are Monday-Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Additional hours if/when needed. Special Instructions: Applicants are required to electronically upload a cover letter, resume, copy of transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire), and complete contact information for three references. References will be contacted at a later date. Submission of materials is the applicant's responsibility. Applications without all required materials are incomplete and will not be considered. Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Level P2, Grade 10. Benefits Information: The University offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the accumulation of two vacation days per month and one sick leave day per month, and thirteen University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in a related field (marketing, journalism, communications or similar). Five years of related experience in high‐level communications and an ability to develop messaging to varied audiences through multiple mediums. Ability to work under pressure and ensure that deadlines are strictly met. Highly organized and the ability to triage work assignments so that pressing and urgent matters are managed appropriately. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree from an accredited institution. Experience in a communication related role within higher education or non-profit. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 25929 Posting Date 08/12/2026, 02:50 PM Grade 10 Screening Date: 08/24/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 705 N. Dixie Avenue, Cookeville, TN, 38505, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Accounting Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 07/21/2026 This position is primarily responsible for reconciling all University and Foundation bank accounts in a timely manner. Communication with Business Office personnel is critical to understand the cash management process in Oracle.\nThis position is also responsible for unclaimed property reporting and other financial reconciliations as needed.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Academic Advising Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 05/21/2026 Academic advisor for undergraduate students.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Athletics Training Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 07/24/2026 Assist the Head Athletic Trainer in a NCAA Division I collegiate, coeducational athletic training program.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Laboratory Operations Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/22/2026 Be the First to Apply The Instructional Designer supports faculty and academic programs by applying instructional design principles and best practices to enhance teaching and learning across online, hybrid, and face-to-face modalities. The position provides instructional design consultation, course development support, faculty training, and guidance on educational technologies to promote student success, accessibility, and effective learning experiences. \n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. See More Jobs Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unle