    "https://fa-eygi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/25711": {
      "title": "Grants Specialist (Grants Admin Specialist II)",
      "description": "Grants Specialist (Grants Admin Specialist II) - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Grants Specialist (Grants Admin Specialist II) Cookeville, TN, United States Job Description Description of Job Duty: The overall purpose of this position is to manage numerous externally funded grant budgets and to provide administrative and analytic support to the Water Center. Work with faculty, staff, students, and external constituents, as appropriate, to review and monitor award expenditures to ensure compliance with grant award terms and conditions. This position will also provide additional budgetary and compliance support to the Water Center as needed. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Provide pre-award and post-award support for all proposals and grant related activities across all the Water Center related projects in compliance with applicable policies and regulations. Interpret policies, contracts, plans, objectives, rules and regulations, apply judgment and develop and implement procedures. Provide budgetary management of proposals and awards Interface and communicate effectively with faculty, staff, various offices in the University and external funding agencies to review, analyze and interpret proposals and award documents. Participate in and collaborate in internal and external audits and project investigations. Prepare reports and budget data for University units as needed. Manage and monitor fund balances and expenses and prepare budget revisions, account corrections and labor reallocations as needed. Facilitate hiring and processing of payroll, summer/extra pay, and release time for personnel related to grants. Process grant activations and finalize closeouts according to TTU policies and agency guidelines. Provide administrative support in the development and submission of grant proposals to funding agencies, especially those projects that are directly aligned with the focus areas of the Water Center. Perform other duties related to proposals and award management as assigned. Approve monthly procard reallocations for grant indexes on Water Center issued procards. Request proper documentation for all charges on monthly statements. Assist Water Center Manager with analytical and administrative support. Analyze, assemble and provide requested data for fiscal report. Assist with generating budgets. Work on special projects as assigned. Develop and implement new procedures for stream-lining Water Center functions. Place and receive Water Center or lab orders as needed. Process Water Center student payroll/GA paperwork when needed. Assist with arranging and/or serving as support for special meetings and events. Provide backup for Water Center manager in his/her absence. Physical Demands: Those typical to perform the job duties listed. Work Hours: Typical hours are Monday-Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Special Instructions: Applicants are required to electronically upload a cover letter, resume, copy of transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire), and complete contact information for three references. References will be contacted at a later date. Submission of materials is the applicant’s responsibility. Applications without all required materials are incomplete and will not be considered. Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Level P2, Grade 10. Benefits Information: The University offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the accumulation of two vacation days per month, one sick leave day per month, and thirteen University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution with one year of related professional experience, or an associate's/60 credit hours with three years of related professional experience. Effective communication skills. Experience with software such as word processing, spreadsheets, and databases. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, staff, and the public. Ability to multi-task. Professional experience in accounting and/or contract/budget administration. Project management skills are needed, as well as ability to interpret policies and guidelines related to proposals and award management. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or higher from an accredited institution. Three to five years of related professional experience. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 25711 Posting Date 08/04/2026, 02:11 PM Grade 10 Screening Date: 09/08/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 200 W. 10th Street, Cookeville, TN, 38505, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Accounting Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 07/21/2026 This position is primarily responsible for reconciling all University and Foundation bank accounts in a timely manner. Communication with Business Office personnel is critical to understand the cash management process in Oracle.\nThis position is also responsible for unclaimed property reporting and other financial reconciliations as needed.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Academic Advising Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 05/21/2026 Academic advisor for undergraduate students.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Athletics Training Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 07/24/2026 Assist the Head Athletic Trainer in a NCAA Division I collegiate, coeducational athletic training program.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Public Relations Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 08/12/2026 Lead the development and execution of strategic communications, engagement, and stewardship initiatives that strengthen relationships with alumni, donors, and other key constituents. This position oversees Advancement communications across print, digital, email, web, and social media platforms; manages donor stewardship communications; and supports the University's fundraising and engagement goals through effective messaging, content development, and leadership within Crawford Alumni Center.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. See More Jobs Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Grants Specialist (Grants Admin Specialist II) - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers loaded"
