    "https://fa-eygi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/25800": {
      "title": "Systems Analyst (Enterprise Application Services Specialist II)",
      "description": "Systems Analyst (Enterprise Application Services Specialist II) - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Systems Analyst (Enterprise Application Services Specialist II) Cookeville, TN, United States Trending Job Description Description of Job Duty: The overall purpose of this job is to provide support for Tennessee Tech University's administrative enterprise systems, including Ellucian Banner, Oracle Fusion, and other third-party applications as assigned. The role primarily focuses on application configuration management, application development, end-user technical support, analytics, ad-hoc reporting, and driving projects that enhance mission-critical systems. Additionally, this position serves as the technical support lead for designated administrative units, ensuring efficient and effective system operation. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Perform application configuration management, application development, and technical support for Ellucian Banner, Oracle Fusion, and third-party systems as assigned. Analyze business processes and make relevant recommendations for improvement. Build reports, forms, analytic dashboards, and automation to streamline business processes, improving efficiency and data accessibility. Analyze user-reported problems and issues and provide resolutions or develop solutions as needed. Act as the liaison between functional users and vendors to resolve technical issues when internal solutions are not available. Develop and support unit testing, ensuring the integrity of the systems. Provide timely status reports to functional users and management regarding project progress. Participate in planning sessions for implementing system upgrades or adding new features. Physical Demands: Those typical of an office environment. Work Hours: Typical hours are 8:00am-4:30pm Monday through Friday. Additional hours as needed. Special Instructions: Applicants are required to electronically upload a cover letter, resume, copy of transcripts (official transcripts may be required upon hire), and complete contact information for three professional references. References will be contacted at a later date. Submission of materials is the applicant's responsibility. Applications without all required materials are incomplete and will not be considered. Salary: Level P2, Grade 12. Benefits Information: The University offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the accumulation of two vacation days per month, one sick leave day per month, and thirteen University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in Computer Science, Information Systems, Management Information Systems, Business Administration, Data Science or similar fields. At least one year of recent technical support experience, particularly in an end-user support role. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in a higher education environment is preferred. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 25800 Posting Date 07/24/2026, 11:33 AM Grade 12 Screening Date: 08/04/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 1010 N Peachtree Ave, Cookeville, TN, 38505, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Senior Business Intelligence Architect (Enterprise Applications Services Specialist IV) Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 08/19/2026 The Senior Business Intelligence Architect is responsible for designing, governing, and evolving the University's business intelligence ecosystem to ensure institutional data is accurate, secure, accessible, and actionable for decision-making. This position serves as the University's lead architect for enterprise analytics solutions, supporting applications including but not limited to Banner, Oracle Fusion Cloud, Ellucian Insights, Power BI, and other institutional reporting platforms while promoting data governance, reporting standards, and analytics modernization initiatives across the campus community.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Systems Analyst (Enterprise Application Services Specialist II) - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers loaded"
