      "description": "Athletics Training Specialist II - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Athletics Training Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Job Description Description of Job Duty: Assist the Head Athletic Trainer in a NCAA Division I collegiate, coeducational athletic training program. Specific duties include supervising the treatment and rehabilitation of athletic injuries, assisting with physical examinations, supervising graduate students, providing athletic trainer coverage of athletic practices and contests, to include travel with assigned athletic teams, and assisting with administrative duties. Sporting assignment will be with Men's Basketball and Men's Golf. Performs other duties as assigned. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Assist the Head Athletic Trainer in a NCAA Division I collegiate, coeducational athletic training program. Specific duties include supervising the treatment and rehabilitation of athletic injuries, assisting with physical examinations, supervising graduate students, providing athletic trainer coverage of athletic practices and contests, to include travel with assigned athletic teams, and assisting with administrative duties. Sporting assignment will be with Men's Basketball and Men's Golf. Performs other duties as assigned. Physical Demands: Physically Demanding; Some Lifting (tape injured players, etc.) Long Times on Feet. Work Hours: Before Hours; After Hours; Weekend Work Required Special Instructions: Applicants will be required to submit a cover letter, resume, contact information for three professional references, and a copy of unofficial transcripts (official transcripts will be required upon hire). Submission of materials is the applicant’s responsibility. Applications without all required materials are incomplete and will not be considered. Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Level P2, Grade 8. Benefits Information: The University offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the accumulation of two vacation days per month, one sick leave day per month, and thirteen University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. Minimum of one year of athletic training experience. National Athletic Trainers Association Board of Certification \"national\" certification required. Tennessee Athletic Trainers \"state\" license or eligibility for license. Beyond meeting minimum requirements, candidates will be evaluated in terms of how their experience and education have prepared them for serving as an assistant athletic trainer in a NCAA Division I collegiate, coeducational athletic training program. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with intercollegiate student-athletes. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 25808 Posting Date 07/24/2026, 11:28 AM Grade 8 Screening Date: 08/03/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 1160 N. Peachtree Avenue, Cookeville, TN, 38505, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Accounting Specialist II Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 07/21/2026 This position is primarily responsible for reconciling all University and Foundation bank accounts in a timely manner. Communication with Business Office personnel is critical to understand the cash management process in Oracle.\nThis position is also responsible for unclaimed property reporting and other financial reconciliations as needed.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/