    "https://fa-eygi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/25701": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Economics",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Economics - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor of Economics Cookeville, TN, United States Trending Job Description Description of Job Duty: POSITION DESCRIPTION : full -time , tenure-track position at the Assistant/Associate Professor rank starting in August 2027. Teaching responsibilities at the undergraduate and/or M.B.A. levels. All areas of interest will be considered. THE COLLEGE: Serving 1,400 students, Tennessee Tech’s College of Business holds AACSB accreditation and offers undergraduate degrees and majors in Economics, Finance, Marketing, Management, Decision Sciences, and Accounting.  Beginning in Fall of 2027, the College of Business will house the Behavioral Research Lab, in which faculty and students can conduct and participate in laboratory experiments. The BS in Economics is a STEM-designated degree that focuses on the quantitative aspects of economics along with an emphasis in econometrics. The College also offers graduate degrees in Business (M.B.A.) and Accounting ( MAcc ), as well a range of minors and certificates. THE UNIVERSITY : Serving around 10,700 students, Tennessee Technological University is located in Cookeville - one hour from Nashville and situated in the Upper Cumberland Region of Middle Tennessee. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Tennessee Technological University and the College of Business emphasize quality teaching and mentoring. The standard teaching load is 9 credit hours (3 courses) per semester and courses may be taught in traditional, online, or hybrid formats. Research leading to refereed publications is required. Service to the university and the profession are expected. Physical Demands: Those typical of an office or classroom environment. Special Instructions: Applicants must apply online and electronically upload the following: Letter of application Curriculum vitae Job market paper (uploaded as Sample of Recent Research document) Teaching evaluations Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts will be required upon hire) Contact information for three references Submission of materials is the applicant’s responsibility. Applications without all required materials are considered incomplete and will not be considered.  Screening begins November 22, 2026. The position will remain open until filled. Salary: Competitive with AACSB-accredited peer institutions and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Benefits Information: Tennessee Tech offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the accumulation of one (1) sick leave day per month and thirteen (13) University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Deferred income and benefits over 12 months. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Ph .D. in Economics or equivalent from an accredited institution. A.B.D.s in advanced dissertation stages will also be considered, but the degree must be conferred by the start date (August 1, 2027). Candidates should demonstrate the potential for excellent teaching, research, and service to the university and profession. Candidates must demonstrate the ability to teach online and teach alternative delivery formats. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience at the principles and intermediate level. Candidates who are eager to develop and teach a senior -level elective in their area of expertise are welcomed. JOE Signals will be considered. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 25701 Posting Date 07/23/2026, 09:25 AM Grade 0 Screening Date: 11/22/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 1105 N. Peachtree Avenue, Cookeville, TN, 38505, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 06/29/2026 Trending The Department of Accounting in the College of Business at Tennessee Technological University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank beginning August 1, 2027. Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor of Social Work (MSW Faculty / Clinical Therapist) Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/18/2026 Be the First to Apply The Department of Sociology and Political Science at Tennessee Tech University invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor of Social Work beginning August 1, 2027.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Assistant Professor Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 08/12/2026 Trending Full-time, tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor rank starting in August 2027. Assistant Professor Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/15/2026 Be the First to Apply Assistant Professor of Violin/Viola\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. See More Jobs Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Assistant/Associate Professor of Economics - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers loaded"
