    "https://fa-eygi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/25667": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers Skip to main content. Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting Cookeville, TN, United States Trending Job Description Description of Job Duty: The Department of Accounting in the College of Business at Tennessee Technological University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank beginning August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate accounting courses, maintain an active program of scholarship, and participate in service activities consistent with AACSB accreditation standards. Appointment at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank will be based on qualifications, experience, teaching effectiveness and scholarly accomplishments. Tennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Responsibilities Essential Functions: Tennessee Tech emphasizes excellence in teaching and student mentoring.  the normal teaching load is three courses (9 credit hours) per semester.  Faculty teach undergraduate and graduate courses in classroom, online, and hybrid formats. Faculty are expected to maintain an active research agenda leading to peer-reviewed publications, provide high-quality instruction, mentor students, and contribute service to the department, university, profession, and business community.  Summer teaching opportunities may be available based on departmental needs and funding. Tennessee Tech provides impact through engaged students, dedicated faculty, and career-ready graduates known for creativity, tenacity, and analytical problem solving. Physical Demands: Those typical of an office or classroom environment. Special Instructions: Applicants must apply electronically through the Tennessee Tech employment website (tntech.edu/jobs) and submit: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement Teaching statement Evidence of teaching effectiveness Sample of recent research or job market paper Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire) Contact information for three professional references Applications will be reviewed beginning September 7, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Submission of materials is the applicant’s responsibility. Applications without all required documents are incomplete and will not be considered. Individuals interested in connecting with department representatives or having questions about the position may contact Dr. Robert Wilbanks (rwilbanks@tntech.edu) or Dr. Richard Rand (richardrand@tntech.edu). Initial interviews will be conducted virtually.  Finalists will be invited for campus interviews during Fall 2026. Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Full-time, nine-month, tenure-track position to begin August 1, 2027. Benefits Information: Tennessee Tech offers a competitive benefits package. Benefits include the accumulation of one (1) sick leave day per month and thirteen (13) University holidays. Other benefits include medical and life insurance (shared cost with the university), retirement, optional 401k, and educational benefits. Deferred income and benefits over 12 months. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Earned Ph.D. or DBA in Accounting from an AACSB-accredited institution or a school with internationally recognized accreditation. ABD candidates in advanced stages of dissertation completion will be considered, however, all degree requirements must be completed by August 1, 2027. Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service consistent with AACSB accreditation standards. Preferred Qualifications: Ability or strong potential to teach undergraduate and graduate auditing courses. Professional accounting experience in public accounting, industry, government, or related settings. Evidence of effective teaching and student engagement. Evidence of scholarly productivity and research potential. Experience teaching in face-to-face, online, and/or hybrid environments. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 25667 Posting Date 06/29/2026, 01:41 PM Grade 0 Screening Date: 09/07/2026 © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 242 E. 10th Street, Cookeville, TN, 38505, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor of Economics Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 07/23/2026 Trending Full-time, tenure-track position at the Assistant/Associate Professor rank starting in August 2027. Teaching responsibilities at the undergraduate and/or M.B.A. levels. All areas of interest will be considered.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor of Social Work (MSW Faculty / Clinical Therapist) Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/18/2026 Be the First to Apply The Department of Sociology and Political Science at Tennessee Tech University invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor of Social Work beginning August 1, 2027.\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Assistant Professor Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 08/12/2026 Trending Full-time, tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor rank starting in August 2027. Assistant Professor Cookeville, TN, United States Posted on 09/15/2026 Be the First to Apply Assistant Professor of Violin/Viola\n\nTennessee Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. See More Jobs Tennessee Tech Homepage Human Resources Pay Grade Table I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting - Tennessee Tech Careers Careers loaded"
